{
  "name": "every invalid_role names the field it is about",
  "description": "ADR-0024 decision 16 and RFC-0024 §5's first table, which the ADR adopts as the mapping.\n\nThe service already wrote a sentence for every refusal and the controller dropped it, so every role refusal reached the client as the same bare `invalid_role` and the form could not say what was wrong. Now each carries `field`, the request key it is about, and `position` when that key is a list. The CODE is unchanged, so nothing that branches on it breaks, and the sentence is still not sent — a client words its own; `field` is what lets it put the words beside the right control.\n\nOne row of the table per step, each request wrong in exactly one way and otherwise valid, locations included — so no other rule can answer first. The five that roles/an_open_role_is_immutable already asserts (base above the package, an amount with no currency, other with no note, superseded, hired_via_platform naming nobody) are not repeated; the contact route's `tentative_result_date` is asserted by roles/candidates_are_staged_then_contacted and is unchanged.\n\nFreelance pays by the hour and everything else by the year (ADR-0019), so the hourly rows use a freelance role. An unknown key and a mistyped value are 400 rather than 422 and name the key; nothing here writes a role, and the settings stay at their defaults. A list key names the item by `position`, 1-based (amendment 1 §1.6).",
  "seed": ["principals"],
  "steps": [
    {
      "_step": "No title — whitespace is not one.",
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/org-roles/01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000b001/roles",
        "body": {
          "title": "   ",
          "engagement": "full_time",
          "locations": [
            {
              "mode": "remote"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 422,
        "body": {
          "error": "invalid_role",
          "field": "title"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "Not one of the four engagements.",
      "as": "hank",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/org-roles/01920000-0000-7000-8000-00000000b001/roles",
        "body": {
          "title": "Platform engineer",
          "engagement": "permanent",
          "locations": [
            {
              "mode": "remote"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 422,
        "body": {
          "error": "invalid_role",
          "field": "engagement"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "_step": "An amount with a currency that is not a three-letter code.",
